DUPLICATE of #55, which was filed minutes earlier for the same failure from
the same live Docker run. Closed in favour of #55; act there.

Both describe: t/secrets_configs.t dying with 503 "This node is not a swarm
manager" against a plain single-node Docker install, because Docker serves
/secrets and /configs only on a swarm manager while Podman serves them from
its own local store.

#55 additionally records that the fix must be a skip rather than a
`docker swarm init`, and that the failure is a die rather than a failed
assertion, so it takes the whole file down.
